This crate implements FT8 from the published protocol description:
S. Franke, B. Somerville and J. Taylor, "The FT4 and FT8 Communication
Protocols", QEX, July/August 2020. It contains no WSJT-X source code.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party material
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ft8_lib — https://github.com/kgoba/ft8_lib (commit 9fec6ca398)

  Consulted: ft8_lib's CRC, message packing, encoder (LDPC encoding and
  tone mapping) and waveform code.
  Copied: the (174,91) LDPC generator matrix and parity-check matrix
  (src/ldpc_tables.rs), transcribed mechanically from ft8/constants.c.
  Followed: the waveform's extension of the first and last tone beyond the
  transmission (src/waveform/mod.rs), which the QEX paper does not specify.
  Taken from it: the callsign-hash multiplier 47 055 833 459 and the order
  of the 38-character callsign alphabet, which the QEX paper defers to
  reference programs it does not print (the free-text alphabet is printed
  in the paper and matches). The standard-call character sets match.
  The CRC, packing, LDPC encoding, tone mapping and synthesis code was
  written from the QEX paper; no ft8_lib function was translated. The tables and hash multiplier
  originate in WSJT-X; they are interoperability constants of the protocol,
  used here as facts.

